    "body": "This change I think could become a problem, because it means that the promise will be resolved before the event is fired, and the order relative to other events could change. For the most part, the spec currently makes sure that there's a single task where observable state (`error`) is changed, the event is fired and then promises are rejected or resolved. At least I find it easier to reason about things when that is upheld.\n\nWill comment separately on other options.\n",
